    "type": "standard",
    "description": "<p><em>A pulsating pool of gray, unstable biomass overflows into reality, spawning short-lived organic horrors.</em></p><h3>Manifest</h3><p>The Entity materializes as a separate, physical creature on the battlefield. The creature has the stats listed by your Entity. The following rules apply:</p><ul><li><p>While within Far range, you can command the creature with a Power Trait Roll (attack, interact with environment as per GM choice).</p></li><li><p>When the creature takes damage, you must mark your Hit Points depending on the severity of the damage. You can <strong>spend an Echo</strong> to reduce the severity by one threshold; there is no other way to reduce the damage taken. After they take damage, you can choose to dismiss them.</p></li><li><p>The creature has traits and features depending on its type. Evasion and Damage Thresholds scale according to the character’s tier: Tier 1 | 2 | 3 | 4.</p></li></ul><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Evasion</th><th>Damage Thresholds</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tier 1</td><td>9</td><td>8/16</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 2</td><td>10</td><td>13/26</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 3</td><td>11</td><td>18/36</td></tr><tr><td>Tier 4</td><td>12</td><td>23/48</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Parasitic Tendrils:</strong> Very Close | <strong>d10 + Power Trait</strong> kinetic damage using your Proficiency</p><h3>Vessel</h3><p>The Entity inhabits your character, merging directly with your physical body. You gain the benefits listed by your Entity.</p><p><em>Your genetic matrix destabilizes, causing your flesh to weep corrupting matter and sprout temporary appendages.</em></p><p>All other creatures within Melee range have disadvantage on attack rolls. In addition, you can make an attack roll against a target within Very Close range. On a success, <strong>spend an Echo</strong> to deal <strong>d8 + Power Trait</strong> kinetic damage using your Proficiency and make them become temporarily <em>Weakened</em>.</p>",
